  ('gi-illuga', 'genshin-impact', 'Illuga', 'https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/gensin-impact/images/9/96/Illuga_Icon.png', '4', 'Geo', 90, null, null, null, null, false, 'A member of the Lightkeepers'' investigation squad, the Nightmare Orioles, he is much like the lantern he carries — both a guiding light and a source of care.

Spring in Nod-Krai is cruel.

Unlike the Northlands, where snow blankets the earth through all four seasons, denying even a glimmer of hope to the life buried beneath, the spring in Nod-Krai ushers in a false sense of optimism.

As the bitter winter loosens its grip, the frost melts into the thirsty soil, and seeds buried deep since the year before drink once more of the sweet, damp earth. They sense warmth above and stir, believing the frigid foe who shattered their stems and leaves has vanished with the passing of time — spurred by that fleeting promise, tender sprouts strain to push through the cracked earth and taste the air above.

But it is all a lie — a trap woven for the unwary.', 'https://genshin-impact.fandom.com/wiki/Illuga%2FProfile', 'A member of the Lightkeepers'' investigation squad, the Nightmare Orioles, he is much like the lantern he carries — both a guiding light and a source of care.

Spring in Nod-Krai is cruel.

Unlike the Northlands, where snow blankets the earth through all four seasons, denying even a glimmer of hope to the life buried beneath, the spring in Nod-Krai ushers in a false sense of optimism.

As the bitter winter loosens its grip, the frost melts into the thirsty soil, and seeds buried deep since the year before drink once more of the sweet, damp earth. They sense warmth above and stir, believing the frigid foe who shattered their stems and leaves has vanished with the passing of time — spurred by that fleeting promise, tender sprouts strain to push through the cracked earth and taste the air above.

But it is all a lie — a trap woven for the unwary.', 'https://genshin-impact.fandom.com/wiki/Illuga%2FProfile', '"Illuga está muy agradecido por la ayuda de los Caballeros de Favonius durante la batalla. Lamentablemente, tuvo que partir a otra misión de investigación, así que me pidió que te entregara esta botella de vino como muestra de su gratitud".

“Jajaja, qué amable es ese muchacho. En realidad, él fue quien más duro trabajó. Ah, qué lástima que no esté aquí, así no voy a poder rechazar su regalo... ¿Qué tal si abrimos la botella aquí mismo? Así puedo hablarte del brillante futuro que le espera a Illuga”.

"Je, podemos beber si quieres, pero no aproveches para robarme al personal".
Para cada nuevo miembro que se une a los Lampareros, no hay mayor fortuna que tener a alguien como Illuga como líder.', 'https://genshin-impact.fandom.com/es/wiki/Illuga%2FHistoria', false, '[{"desde":20,"hasta":40,"creditos":20000,"materiales":[{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_101269.png","nombre":"Ámbar de pino","cantidad":3},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_104171.png","nombre":"Pedacito de topacio prithiva","cantidad":1},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_112122.png","nombre":"Eje dañado","cantidad":3}]},{"desde":40,"hasta":50,"creditos":40000,"materiales":[{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_101269.png","nombre":"Ámbar de pino","cantidad":10},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_104172.png","nombre":"Fragmento de topacio prithiva","cantidad":3},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_112122.png","nombre":"Eje dañado","cantidad":15},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_113080.png","nombre":"Núcleo kuuvahki de bucle militar","cantidad":2}]},{"desde":50,"hasta":60,"creditos":60000,"materiales":[{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_101269.png","nombre":"Ámbar de pino","cantidad":20},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_104172.png","nombre":"Fragmento de topacio prithiva","cantidad":6},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_112123.png","nombre":"Eje reforzado","cantidad":12},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_113080.png","nombre":"Núcleo kuuvahki de bucle militar","cantidad":4}]},{"desde":60,"hasta":70,"creditos":80000,"materiales":[{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_101269.png","nombre":"Ámbar de pino","cantidad":30},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_104173.png","nombre":"Trozo de topacio prithiva","cantidad":3},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_112123.png","nombre":"Eje reforzado","cantidad":18},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_113080.png","nombre":"Núcleo kuuvahki de bucle militar","cantidad":8}]},{"desde":70,"hasta":80,"creditos":100000,"materiales":[{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_101269.png","nombre":"Ámbar de pino","cantidad":45},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_104173.png","nombre":"Trozo de topacio prithiva","cantidad":6},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_112124.png","nombre":"Eje refinado","cantidad":12},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_113080.png","nombre":"Núcleo kuuvahki de bucle militar","cantidad":12}]},{"desde":80,"hasta":90,"creditos":120000,"materiales":[{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_101269.png","nombre":"Ámbar de pino","cantidad":60},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_104174.png","nombre":"Topacio prithiva","cantidad":6},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_112124.png","nombre":"Eje refinado","cantidad":24},{"icono":"https://gi.yatta.moe/assets/UI/UI_ItemIcon_113080.png","nombre":"Núcleo kuuvahki de bucle militar","cantidad":20}]}]'::jsonb),
  ('gi-ineffa', 'genshin-impact', 'Ineffa', 'https://enka.network/ui/UI_AvatarIcon_Ineffa.png', '5', 'Electro', 90, null, 'DPS', null, null, false, 'A robot from Nod-Krai constructed using mechanical components from all over the world. She was designed and built at the Clink-Clank Krumkake Craftshop.

Regarding mechanical life forms and their "sense of self," a scholar once proposed the following thought experiment: Suppose a machine''s parts age and are replaced each day. In time, all of its parts will have been replaced, and none of its original components will remain. At that point, is that machine still its original "self"?

This question never seemed to pose much of a problem for Ineffa: No matter how many times her outer shell or components were replaced, her "core" had always remained the same. Ineffa''s core was quite literally her home.

But what would happen if her core were ever dismantled in some way? Which part would represent her then? Even though Ineffa''s maker did not yet possess the technological skill, she had always yearned to take apart Ineffa''s core and analyze it.', 'https://genshin-impact.fandom.com/wiki/Ineffa%2FProfile', 'A robot from Nod-Krai constructed using mechanical components from all over the world. She was designed and built at the Clink-Clank Krumkake Craftshop.

Regarding mechanical life forms and their "sense of self," a scholar once proposed the following thought experiment: Suppose a machine''s parts age and are replaced each day. In time, all of its parts will have been replaced, and none of its original components will remain. At that point, is that machine still its original "self"?

This question never seemed to pose much of a problem for Ineffa: No matter how many times her outer shell or components were replaced, her "core" had always remained the same. Ineffa''s core was quite literally her home.

But what would happen if her core were ever dismantled in some way? Which part would represent her then? Even though Ineffa''s maker did not yet possess the technological skill, she had always yearned to take apart Ineffa''s core and analyze it.', 'https://genshin-impact.fandom.com/wiki/Ineffa%2FProfile', '"Antes que nada, ¡hay que reconocer que Ineffa es la mejor robot del mundo! Luego, hay que saber respetar sus opiniones y decisiones. Además, el derecho de interpretación final le pertenece al Taller de Krumkake Cling... Eh, ¡quiero decir, a Ineffa!".
Que los humanos hayan intentado emular el funcionamiento de la vida a través de mecanismos y engranajes no es una ocurrencia poco común en la historia de Teyvat.

Khaenri''ah abrió la tierra con gigantes forjados de acero, y el rey de la mecánica dio paso a una nueva era con mecanismos propulsados con mecatecnología.

Tal vez, a ojos de algunos locos, la humanidad no sea más que una máquina construida con carne y huesos.

Si echamos la vista a los creadores de las cosas no humanas y llevamos los límites más allá de las creaciones mecánicas...

Nos daremos cuenta de que los dioses se adentraron en el Mar Primigenio y los pecadores se lanzaron al Abismo, igual que el antiguo Rey Dragón grabó su consciencia y su alma en el flogisto.

